      "knowledge_point": "Finding a Difference of Sets Without a Venn Diagram",
      "problem": "If $C=\\{-3,-1,0,5,10\\}$ and $D=\\{-2,-1,0,1\\}$, then $C∖D=$",
      "worked_solution": "The set $C∖D$ is the set of all elements belonging to $C$ but *not* $D.$ Note that the elements $-1,0\\in D$ are also in $C,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & =\\{-3,-1,0,5,10\\}-\\{-2,-1,0,1\\} \\\\  & =\\{-3,5,10\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
